---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import site from "../../data/site.json";
---

<BaseLayout title={`Portfolio | ${site.siteName}`} description={`${site.siteName}'s portfolio: CRM consulting, Dynamics 365 CE, Power Platform, certifications, education, and project strengths.`}>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero portrait-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio</p>
        <h1>CRM, Power Platform, and business analysis in one practical profile.</h1>
        <p>I help teams turn business needs into clear CRM workflows, delivery-ready requirements, and systems that people can use every day.</p>
      </div>
      <img src="/assets/headshot-professional.jpg" alt={`${site.siteName} professional portrait`} />
    </section>

    <section class="section detail-grid">
      <article><span>Current focus</span><h3>Dynamics 365 CE and Power Platform</h3><p>CRM modernization, service workflows, sales operations, automation, reporting, and adoption.</p></article>
      <article><span>Education</span><h3>Southwest Jiaotong University</h3><p>Founded in 1896, SWJTU is known for engineering and transportation disciplines. That background shaped how I think about systems, process, and scale.</p></article>
      <article><span>Professional setting</span><h3>Canadian business systems work</h3><p>My recent work is centered on CRM, customer operations, and system modernization in Canadian business contexts.</p></article>
      <article><span>Certifications</span><h3>Microsoft business applications path</h3><p>Dynamics 365 CE, Customer Service, Power Platform, Dataverse, Power Automate, and solution delivery practices.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="section split-section">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>How I usually add value.</h2></div>
      <div class="copy-block">
        <p>I clarify the real workflow behind a request: who owns the data, where handoffs happen, what exceptions matter, and what users need to see when they make decisions.</p>
        <p>Then I turn that into useful delivery artifacts: user stories, acceptance criteria, process maps, CRM behavior, automation rules, test scenarios, and rollout notes.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Strengths</p><h2>Where I tend to be useful.</h2></div>
      <div class="soft-card-grid">
        <article><h3>Business process discovery</h3><p>Finding the real process behind the system request.</p></article>
        <article><h3>CRM functional design</h3><p>Turning sales, service, and customer records into usable CRM behavior.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Power Platform automation</h3><p>Replacing repetitive manual work with controlled, explainable workflows.</p></article>
        <article><h3>User adoption</h3><p>Helping business users understand why a new system makes daily work easier.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
